# Amendment #28 — workspace-identity-routed first-run
#
# 2026-04-23. Closes the pos3/ivers-corp-pos-v2 false-success
# mode: one host with two pos-v2 workspaces, `~/.pos/first-run.state`
# written by workspace A, workspace B's SessionStart hook
# short-circuited to `_msg_completed()` because the state-file
# sentinel had no workspace identity. B's .venv/, plists, and
# self-retired settings.json were all missing; the hook claimed
# "pos-v2 first-run completed" anyway. Re-extension of amendment
# #6's AC6 per ODD §4 — AC6 exercised the scaffold layer on both
# workspaces correctly but bypassed the dispatcher layer that
# reads the global state file and decides whether to invoke the
# scaffold at all.
#
# Structural remedy (Option C from research §5.3): first-run
# state moves from `~/.pos/first-run.state` (host-global) to
# `<workspace>/.pos/first-run.state` (workspace-local). Workspace
# identity is enforced by path; no dispatcher-side "remember to
# check workspace" advisory. Defence in depth: `FirstRunState`
# gains a `workspace_root: str` field; the dispatcher refuses a
# state whose recorded workspace does not match the current
# `pos_v2_root` (handles the path-moved-by-admin edge case).
