# Amendment #29 — per-workspace memory-sidecar port + workspace-identity health probe
#
# 2026-04-24. Closes the second workspace-identity sibling in the
# memory-sidecar surface: two pos-v2 workspaces on one host could
# not run their memory sidecars concurrently because both bound
# the hardcoded TCP port 127.0.0.1:8765 and the second-booted
# sidecar crashloops on `[Errno 48] address already in use`. The
# third sibling (workspace-identity at the /health probe layer)
# was folded in as AC29.5 per owner ruling D6 (2026-04-24): the
# probe had no way to confirm that a 200 response on the probed
# port actually came from *this* workspace's sidecar as opposed
# to an orphan or another workspace's.
#
# Re-extension of amendment #6's AC6 per ODD §4 (precedent set by
# amendment #28 which closed the state-file-routing sibling of
# the same family). No spec v1.x amendment per owner ruling D1.
#
# Structural remedy (S1 per research §7.1):
#  - The scaffold's `memory.yaml` seam is the port-propagation
#    source of truth. Scaffold reads `port` from
#    `~/.pos/memory.yaml` (falling through the starter default
#    when pre-seeded by a prior scaffold), and writes
#    `GRAPHITI_SERVICE_PORT` into the launchd plist's
#    `EnvironmentVariables` dict alongside the pre-existing
#    `PYTHONUNBUFFERED`. The sidecar's `service.py` env-var read
#    already reached for `GRAPHITI_SERVICE_PORT` (amendment #24
#    AC24.6); this amendment is the consumer wiring that lets
#    the env var actually reach the sidecar in the non-test
#    path.
#  - The `/health` response body gains a `workspace_root` field
#    populated from `POS_V2_WORKSPACE_ROOT` (also injected via
#    the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`). Hands-off-lifecycle's
#    phase-4b probe verifies the body's `workspace_root` matches
#    the dispatching workspace's own root; mismatch is treated
#    as "not healthy" and surfaces in the pending-services
#    diagnostic.
#
# Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):
#  - Port source: scaffold writes the starter default (8765)
#    into every fresh `memory.yaml`; distinct workspaces on one
#    host require the operator (or a future Idea 9 cycle) to
#    edit one workspace's `memory.yaml` to a different port.
#    The amendment lands the propagation seam, not a port-
#    derivation policy — AC29.3 verifies the seam by
#    pre-seeding distinct values per-workspace rather than
#    asserting a derivation formula. Slug-derivation remains
#    a future Idea 9 scope.
#  - Workspace identity source: `POS_V2_WORKSPACE_ROOT` env var
#    injected via launchd plist's `EnvironmentVariables`. Empty
#    string is the explicit "unknown" value; the probe treats
#    mismatch-or-missing as structural failure.
#
# Fail-closed behaviours:
#  - /health probe with mismatched workspace_root → probe
#    reports not-healthy → phase-4b times out → user sees the
#    service-health-timeout diagnostic (no silent success on an
#    orphan sidecar).
#  - /health probe with absent workspace_root in body → treated
#    as mismatch → same failure path.
#  - Pre-existing `memory.yaml` with `port: 8765` → scaffold
#    respects the existing value; no forced migration
#    (amendment #28 non-migration precedent).
#
# AC surface (AC29.1–AC29.7):
#  - AC29.1: service binds env-var port across distinct values
#    (memory-system).
#  - AC29.2: scaffold propagates memory.yaml port → plist +
#    inventory (workspace-bootstrap).
#  - AC29.3: distinct workspace configs → distinct plist ports
